# The character-count ledger: one reviewed row per site that .github/scripts/check-character-counts.sh
# finds, a count beside the word "character", "characters", "char" or "chars" on one line. Read that
# script's header for the rules. Each row is tab-separated: the path; the SHA-256 of the line's exact
# bytes; the occurrence's ordinal on the line; which copy of that line in the file it is, from the
# top; the counter that computes the count (`<path>:<symbol>`, or `none` where no code counts it);
# the unit that counter counts (code points, or not a length where the word is no unit of a count);
# and one sentence of why. A row is written by hand from the counter its writer read; nothing writes
# or refreshes rows. `check-character-counts.sh --list` prints each site with its row, and the key
# fields of each row a site needs.
path	line sha-256	occurrence	copy	counter	unit	reason
